    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0813" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4304: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-26T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>98. You are advised as follows in reply to your telegram no. 164 of April 24, 4
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>Arrangements are being made by the Navy Department, in accordance with your
                    suggestion, to land men for reinforcements to the Legation Guard.</p>
                <pb facs="0814" n="694" xml:id="pg694"/>
                <p>Department’s no. 180 of July 16, 1920, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d435-f1"/>
                    will guide you on question of effort of diplomatic corps to prevent military
                    operations about Peking.</p>
                <p>What significance is there in the resignation of Chen?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
